The following JavaScript function is supposed to return the sum of all even numbers in an array, but it returns wrong results. Find the bug, explain it in one sentence, and return the CORRECTED function only.

```js
function sumEven(nums) {
  let total = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i <= nums.length; i++) {
    if (nums[i] % 2 === 0) total += nums[i];
  }
  return total;
}
```

Test case: sumEven([1,2,3,4]) should be 6.
